Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:11:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Web Extensions: what a script adds to a namespace object
 is kept (Sunset W3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A namespace (browser.runtime, browser.webRequest…) is wrapped again when its wrapper has been collected: the wrappers are
cached weakly. What a script added to it (a property, a stand-in) was lost at some later read. Firefox and Chrome keep
them; uBlock Origin relies on it at its start.

The generated getter of an attribute whose type is an extension API object now pins the wrapper it returns to the object
it is read from (JSObjectSetPrivateProperty): the namespace lives as long as browser does. The private property is not
visible to scripts; a permission-dependent (Dynamic) attribute is still read through its getter each time.

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/Extensions/Bindings/Scripts/CodeGeneratorExtensions.pm b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/Extensions/Bindings/Scripts/CodeGeneratorExtensions.pm
index ff03274c9..2fd6abf1e 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/Extensions/Bindings/Scripts/CodeGeneratorExtensions.pm
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/Extensions/Bindings/Scripts/CodeGeneratorExtensions.pm
@@ -945,7 +945,7 @@ JSValueRef ${className}::${getterName}(JSContextRef context, JSObjectRef object,
 {
 EOF
 
-            push(@contents, "    UNUSED_PARAM(propertyName);\n\n");
+            push(@contents, "    UNUSED_PARAM(propertyName);\n\n") unless $attribute->type->name =~ /^WebExtensionAPI/;
 
             push(@contents, <<EOF);
     RefPtr impl = to${implementationClassName}(context, object);
@@ -973,11 +973,24 @@ EOF
                 push(@contents, "    }\n");
             }
 
-            push(@contents, <<EOF);
+            if ($attribute->type->name =~ /^WebExtensionAPI/) {
+                $contentsIncludes{"<JavaScriptCore/JSObjectRefPrivate.h>"} = 1;
+                push(@contents, <<EOF);
+
+    // Kept as long as the object it is read from: what a script adds to it is not lost when its wrapper would be collected.
+    SUPPRESS_UNCOUNTED_ARG JSValueRef result = @{[$self->_returnExpression($attribute, $getterExpression, $interface)]};
+    if (result && JSValueIsObject(context, result))
+        JSObjectSetPrivateProperty(context, object, propertyName, result);
+    return result;
+}
+EOF
+            } else {
+                push(@contents, <<EOF);
 
     SUPPRESS_UNCOUNTED_ARG return @{[$self->_returnExpression($attribute, $getterExpression, $interface)]};
 }
 EOF
+            }
 
             unless ($attribute->isReadOnly) {
                 my $setterEarlyReturnCondition = $earlyReturnCondition;
